Package: ninebark
Title: Type R Commands in Plain English, Right in RStudio
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Dylan", "Winning", email = "dwinning@haverford.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An RStudio Addin that turns a plain-English phrase ("mean of
    1,2,3,4,5", "let x be 5", "read the csv file data.csv into df", "for i
    in 1 to 10 print i") into real R and either runs it in the live Console
    or inserts it into the open Source file. Works identically in RStudio
    Desktop, RStudio Server, Posit Workbench, and Posit Cloud, because it
    talks to the editor only through the official 'rstudioapi' package, not
    by reaching into any one frontend's internals. The natural-language
    resolution itself is the same engine as the Ninebark browser extensions
    for Desmos, Google Sheets, Excel, MATLAB Online, and Overleaf, embedded
    here via the 'V8' package so it runs locally with no network calls and
    no server-side component.
